    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0781" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/21637</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-09T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>683. Department’s telegram 685, January 5, 6 p.m., and Embassy’s 678 January 6,
                    10 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d612-f1"/> I have just received <hi
                        rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> from Acting Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs dated 8th instant, merely stating that the suggestion has been referred
                    to the Subsecretary of War and Marine for such action as he may deem
                    opportune.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
